{"name":"Cloak Grey","hex":"#605e63","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cloak","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long outer garment worn over the shoulders covering the back; a cape, often with a hood.","A blanket-like covering, often metaphorical."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover as with or like a cloak.","To cover up, hide or conceal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cloak"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cloak","blocks":[{"text":"A cloak is a type of loose garment worn over clothing, mostly but not always, as outerwear for outdoor wear, which serves the same purpose as an overcoat and protects the wearer from the weather. It may form part of a uniform. People in many different societies may wear cloaks. Over time, cloak designs have changed to match fashion and available textiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg/330px-Fashion_Plate_Manteau_1823.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloak"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Cloak.jpg/500p